# ── OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ── Editor / IDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .vscode/settings.json is intentionally tracked (shared workspace config).
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Local backups & archives ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The restructure tooling and manual snapshots drop zips next to the repo,
# but catch any that land inside it.
Spinlog-BACKUP-*.zip
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Unoptimised design sources ────────────────────────────────────────
# assets/source/ holds originals that are never served: currently
# "Bike bg.png" (1.9 MB), whose shipped derivative is assets/img/bike-bg.webp.
# Deliberately NOT committed — adding 1.9 MB of dead weight to history would
# need a history rewrite to undo. The files stay on disk locally.
# audit-refs.mjs knows about this folder and exempts it from the orphan check.
assets/source/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This app hardcodes its Supabase anon key in src/js and that is deliberate —
# there is no login, so the key ships in the page and every RLS policy is
# `using (true)`. See "Known limits" and "A note on the key vault" in the README
# for what that does and does not expose. Gemini keys are NOT hardcoded: they live
# on the device and reach the cloud only as AES-256-GCM ciphertext.
# If any of it ever moves to a config file, that file must land here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config.local.js
secrets.json

# ── Node (only if tooling is ever added; there is no build step today) ─
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
package-lock.json.orig

# ── Logs & scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
/tmp/
/.cache/

# ── Layout audit scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/audit-mobile.mjs --shots renders the app in headless Chromium and drops
# PNGs here to look at. They are evidence for one session, not artefacts.
#
# The four audits are tracked. Everything in tools/ whose name starts with an
# underscore is not: that prefix is the convention for a throwaway probe written to
# answer one question — a screenshot differ, a cascade dump, a one-off codemod — and
# a repo with no build step should not accumulate them.
#
# Playwright is likewise not a dependency of the app; see the header of
# audit-mobile.mjs or audit-app.mjs for the two commands that install it.
tools/_*
